WEBVTT

00:01:44.633 --> 00:01:48.533
Thanks to the descendants of
the Soldiers of Light and their efforts,

00:01:48.566 --> 00:01:50.496
the Grankingdom's king Nene,

00:01:50.533 --> 00:01:53.603
who was trying to rule the world
with fear, was defeated.

00:01:55.066 --> 00:02:00.426
The children kidnapped by Nene
were safely released from the Galleon.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.270
And people learned that the long and
painful struggle has come to an end.

00:02:18.833 --> 00:02:19.833
What's wrong?

00:02:20.666 --> 00:02:22.996
I was wondering...

00:02:23.900 --> 00:02:27.430
If we really defeated Nene.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:31.270
Yeah, it's kinda hard
to believe, huh?

00:02:31.766 --> 00:02:33.326
Everyone,
hold your heads high.

00:02:35.033 --> 00:02:36.033
It's our triumphant return.

00:02:36.700 --> 00:02:41.600
THE TRIUMPHANT RETURN

00:02:48.333 --> 00:02:51.033
The survivors from Jibral and

00:02:51.066 --> 00:02:55.426
the countries allied with them
against the Grankingdom

00:02:55.466 --> 00:02:59.196
all traveled to Logic
to celebrate the victory.

00:03:04.333 --> 00:03:06.403
Wow.

00:03:17.700 --> 00:03:20.830
Welcome back, you guys!

00:03:23.966 --> 00:03:25.366
Conrad!

00:03:26.666 --> 00:03:29.026
I can't believe you really
defeated that Nene!

00:03:29.466 --> 00:03:30.966
Good job, Shu!

00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:32.670
Thank you!

00:03:32.933 --> 00:03:34.633
You're not happy to see me?

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.430
There, there...

00:03:36.733 --> 00:03:38.703
I fought well, too.

00:03:38.933 --> 00:03:39.933
Me too.

00:03:43.833 --> 00:03:48.303
Take a look at their faces.
Rejoicing over the peace you've brought.

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:58.203
S-So many people...

00:03:58.566 --> 00:04:01.826
Are they all here to give us
a warm welcome?

00:04:02.266 --> 00:04:03.596
Of course!

00:04:03.933 --> 00:04:06.203
You are heroes who
saved the world.

00:04:06.933 --> 00:04:09.903
That makes me
the heroes' mentor!

00:04:12.166 --> 00:04:14.266
Mentor? Who is?

00:04:14.766 --> 00:04:17.996
We will hold a banquet
to welcome all of you.

00:04:18.533 --> 00:04:19.873
Please relax and
enjoy yourselves.

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:22.370
I want to eat something, maro...

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:24.130
I'm so hungry...

00:04:24.166 --> 00:04:25.166
Me too...

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:31.970
Of course, I personally arranged
great meals to be prepared.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:33.600
- Yay!
- Yay!

00:04:33.666 --> 00:04:36.226
I will escort you to
this castle's grand ballroom.

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.100
Oh wait, where did Zola go?

00:04:44.533 --> 00:04:47.073
You're right. She's gone...

00:04:47.800 --> 00:04:52.530
Oh, Zola said she is going to
leave for a short while.

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.230
She said you guys should
enjoy the reception party.

00:04:56.866 --> 00:04:57.866
What do you mean?

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:04.370
It's okay, it's okay.

00:05:04.833 --> 00:05:07.803
I bet she doesn't like
these formal events.

00:05:08.600 --> 00:05:10.000
Anyway...

00:05:10.033 --> 00:05:12.133
- Feast! Feast!
- Feast! Feast!

00:05:27.266 --> 00:05:30.796
And now, the medal ceremony
led by Pope Vittoria.

00:05:39.633 --> 00:05:46.703
Ahem...and so...
You have brought peace to this world...

00:05:47.266 --> 00:05:52.926
Now, strengthening the army
must be our first priority...

00:05:54.466 --> 00:05:56.466
How long is this gonna last?

00:05:56.900 --> 00:06:00.800
He's talking about things
that are unrelated to us.

00:06:02.933 --> 00:06:04.403
It wasn't me!

00:06:04.733 --> 00:06:05.773
Hey!

00:06:05.966 --> 00:06:07.526
Be quiet!

00:06:11.500 --> 00:06:12.900
You too!

00:06:12.933 --> 00:06:13.933
Shut up!

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.430
I can't hold it anymore, maro.

00:06:20.266 --> 00:06:22.696
I need to go potty, maro!

00:06:22.733 --> 00:06:24.733
- Huh?!
- Huh?!

00:06:25.066 --> 00:06:29.596
Next, is the congratulatory speech
by the king of Amarao Kingdom.

00:06:30.266 --> 00:06:32.096
I'm gonna go potty!

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.273
Marumaro!

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:38.330
Potty, potty, potty,
potty, potty!

00:06:38.366 --> 00:06:39.026
Hey!

00:06:39.066 --> 00:06:40.966
What are you doing?

00:06:42.333 --> 00:06:44.773
Don't stop me, maro!

00:06:45.233 --> 00:06:46.973
Let me go, maro!

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.870
Idiot! Go back to your seat!

00:06:48.900 --> 00:06:51.930
Potty!

00:06:57.933 --> 00:06:58.933
Reporting.

00:06:59.466 --> 00:07:02.826
The surviving forces allied against
the Grankingdom are gathering strength.

00:07:03.366 --> 00:07:07.996
The Grankingdom's forces are
fleeing regardless of their unit size.

00:07:08.866 --> 00:07:10.196
What shall we do now?

00:07:10.733 --> 00:07:14.673
I said we would leave
the Grankingdom.

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.470
But...

00:07:15.700 --> 00:07:16.700
Enough.

00:07:16.933 --> 00:07:18.073
Stay back.

00:07:19.566 --> 00:07:20.226
Yes, sir.

00:07:24.933 --> 00:07:26.333
Maro...

00:07:28.433 --> 00:07:31.303
The hero of justice
is covered in pee...

00:07:31.333 --> 00:07:33.473
Biggest embarrassment
of my life, maro.

00:07:33.800 --> 00:07:36.870
Guys have days like that,
Marumaro.

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:41.430
Don't sympathize with me, maro.
It hurts me even more, maro.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:47.170
By the way, where is Jiro?

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:49.833
Huh? Where did he go?

00:07:51.333 --> 00:07:53.103
Yes, come in.

00:07:56.033 --> 00:07:58.533
Sorry that the ceremony
took so long.

00:07:58.566 --> 00:08:00.296
The meal is ready.

00:08:00.333 --> 00:08:01.833
Yay!

00:08:02.133 --> 00:08:05.273
I can't face everyone
anymore, maro.

00:08:05.566 --> 00:08:09.266
It has to be the biggest embarrassment
in the history of Devee Tribe, maro.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:15.430
Don't worry!
Guys have days like that!

00:08:15.600 --> 00:08:16.630
Maro...

00:08:17.333 --> 00:08:21.033
By the way, what are they doing?
Those people outside the window?

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:24.630
Oh, they're going to go after
the remnants of the Grankingdom Army.

00:08:24.966 --> 00:08:25.966
Now?

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:26.670
Yes.

00:08:26.900 --> 00:08:32.430
Nene is gone, but the Grankingdom's
troops are still out there.

00:08:33.266 --> 00:08:35.166
We are going to get
rid of them completely

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:37.100
before they have
the time to regroup!

00:08:37.433 --> 00:08:41.403
The Grankingdom Army is nothing
without Nene!

00:08:42.033 --> 00:08:45.003
We'll finish them off
in no time!

00:08:45.466 --> 00:08:47.096
You're absolutely right!

00:08:50.366 --> 00:08:52.626
Why are they acting so big?

00:08:52.900 --> 00:08:54.330
Don't know, maro.

00:08:54.566 --> 00:08:57.396
You've all fought really
hard up to this point,

00:08:57.433 --> 00:09:01.273
so we will put in our best effort
to end this fight now.

00:09:01.966 --> 00:09:03.396
Then what about us?

00:09:03.533 --> 00:09:06.403
You should stay here
as long as you want.

00:09:14.833 --> 00:09:15.503
Oh...

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:27.300
Jiro, the meal's ready.

00:09:50.633 --> 00:09:51.633
Here it is.

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:32.100
Eat more! Eat more!

00:10:32.566 --> 00:10:35.896
I'll have the best chefs make
the best meal ever!

00:10:38.533 --> 00:10:40.033
Jiro, are you okay?

00:10:40.200 --> 00:10:40.870
About what?

00:10:41.900 --> 00:10:42.900
Where are you going?

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:44.000
Bathroom.

00:10:44.133 --> 00:10:46.603
You should go pee quick, maro.

00:10:49.833 --> 00:10:52.373
Jiro doesn't seem so good.

00:10:53.366 --> 00:10:55.396
And here we finally
defeated Nene...

00:10:56.266 --> 00:10:57.266
I wonder what's wrong.

00:11:00.900 --> 00:11:03.630
Ah? What's wrong, you guys?

00:11:04.033 --> 00:11:05.933
Eat more! Eat more!

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:08.100
Wow!

00:11:08.766 --> 00:11:10.866
I can't eat that much.

00:11:11.033 --> 00:11:12.033
Yeah...

00:11:12.733 --> 00:11:13.833
What happened?

00:11:14.233 --> 00:11:16.973
Umm, nothing.

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:39.930
These marks left by a sword...

00:11:41.800 --> 00:11:42.800
I knew it.

00:11:57.600 --> 00:12:00.330
That is an unusual request.

00:12:00.800 --> 00:12:05.100
We can do it with
our informant network,

00:12:05.133 --> 00:12:08.233
but it will require time and
considerable amount of money.

00:12:08.433 --> 00:12:10.033
I will pay any amount.

00:12:10.533 --> 00:12:13.803
But just know that
we may not have much time.

00:12:15.500 --> 00:12:18.000
I understand... We'll do it.

00:12:18.633 --> 00:12:19.633
I'm counting on you.

00:12:40.066 --> 00:12:41.066
Won't be that easy.

00:12:49.666 --> 00:12:50.666
There!

00:13:04.666 --> 00:13:06.866
Let me take a look at you.

00:13:14.333 --> 00:13:16.533
Good evening, General Logi.

00:13:21.066 --> 00:13:23.026
Hamburger...

00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:26.270
Boobies...

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:35.430
Underwear...

00:13:36.800 --> 00:13:37.830
Jiro...

00:13:49.400 --> 00:13:50.830
What are you doing?

00:13:52.166 --> 00:13:56.666
Since my hometown was up on a hill,
the moon was more beautiful.

00:13:58.433 --> 00:13:59.803
What, all of a sudden?

00:14:03.533 --> 00:14:06.803
Kluke was worried too,
that you didn't look so well.

00:14:08.333 --> 00:14:09.003
Hey...

00:14:09.500 --> 00:14:10.170
Huh?

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.230
We really
defeated Nene, right?

00:14:13.633 --> 00:14:16.333
Huh? What's wrong,
saying something like that now?

00:14:16.733 --> 00:14:20.803
I've traveled to avenge Nene...
to defeat him.

00:14:22.600 --> 00:14:24.970
But...it feels...

00:14:25.666 --> 00:14:26.326
Huh?

00:14:26.766 --> 00:14:28.226
I thought I'd be happier...

00:14:29.233 --> 00:14:30.933
I thought there'd be more
sense of accomplishment.

00:14:31.733 --> 00:14:34.173
But...now...

00:14:35.400 --> 00:14:39.470
I don't know what to do
from this point...

00:14:40.766 --> 00:14:41.766
What should I do?

00:14:45.833 --> 00:14:47.373
I don't know either.

00:14:48.733 --> 00:14:52.573
We defeated Nene
but it feels weird.

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:54.870
But that doesn't matter.

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:59.870
I will keep protecting those people
and things that I cherish.

00:15:01.433 --> 00:15:02.803
That's not going to change.

00:15:05.100 --> 00:15:06.700
It's so simple for you...

00:15:09.433 --> 00:15:10.673
Delphinium...

00:15:12.300 --> 00:15:13.870
So it was you, after all...

00:15:14.400 --> 00:15:17.130
Since you're coming after me,

00:15:17.166 --> 00:15:20.196
then that means you must've been
Nene's pet all along, correct?

00:15:20.666 --> 00:15:22.226
That's General Logi for you.

00:15:22.766 --> 00:15:24.366
You're very quick.

00:15:24.700 --> 00:15:26.970
I suppose you need
no further explanation.

00:15:27.533 --> 00:15:32.733
You betrayed Lord Nene.
I cannot allow you to get away with it.

00:15:33.366 --> 00:15:36.896
Now that you have failed
to assassinate me,

00:15:36.933 --> 00:15:38.273
what are you going to do?

00:15:43.500 --> 00:15:46.000
We shall meet again.

00:15:46.600 --> 00:15:47.770
Interesting.

00:15:55.800 --> 00:15:56.470
General Logi!

00:15:57.766 --> 00:15:58.766
What happened?

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:03.130
Delphinium tried to
assassinate me.

00:16:03.266 --> 00:16:04.466
W-What?

00:16:04.966 --> 00:16:06.196
I will track her down
immediately!

00:16:09.766 --> 00:16:10.766
That's fine.

00:16:11.166 --> 00:16:13.496
She's probably off
this ship by now.

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:21.370
Fifth Squadron! Sixth Squadron!
At the ready!

00:16:22.700 --> 00:16:23.370
Maro?

00:16:23.800 --> 00:16:26.200
Oh, Marumaro!
Going out to fish?

00:16:26.666 --> 00:16:27.996
Training, maro?

00:16:28.166 --> 00:16:30.966
No, as soon as all the troops arrive,
we're going to attack.

00:16:33.833 --> 00:16:36.203
Being a commander is busy,
so busy.

00:16:38.400 --> 00:16:40.270
Hope you get a good catch!

00:16:49.233 --> 00:16:50.473
I got one!

00:17:20.566 --> 00:17:21.566
Rain...

00:17:23.600 --> 00:17:25.230
It doesn't look like
it's gonna stop.

00:17:27.133 --> 00:17:30.633
Hey, are we going to
stay here forever?

00:17:31.566 --> 00:17:34.696
I don't know what to do, maro.

00:17:35.366 --> 00:17:38.766
Yeah, we always
followed Zola's lead.

00:17:40.566 --> 00:17:43.896
Now that you mention it,
Zola hasn't come back yet.

00:18:00.200 --> 00:18:02.800
Rock... Plop...

00:19:02.833 --> 00:19:04.503
Oh! You guys!

00:19:04.533 --> 00:19:06.973
Conrad!
You're leaving already?

00:19:07.566 --> 00:19:08.796
That's right.

00:19:09.666 --> 00:19:13.126
Take care of yourselves and
please give Zola my best regards.

00:19:13.466 --> 00:19:14.766
Thank you very much.

00:19:15.266 --> 00:19:16.866
Please take care
of yourself, too.

00:19:17.833 --> 00:19:18.503
Yeah.

00:19:34.466 --> 00:19:36.696
Everyone left, maro.

00:19:37.666 --> 00:19:40.226
Hey, what are we
going to do next?

00:19:40.666 --> 00:19:41.866
Who knows...

00:19:41.900 --> 00:19:46.100
There's no need to stay here so
we should each head back home.

00:19:47.266 --> 00:19:47.926
Huh?

00:19:55.233 --> 00:19:59.103
Does that mean
our journey is over?

00:20:01.266 --> 00:20:03.066
Hey, is it?!

00:20:03.266 --> 00:20:05.496
Idiot! Can't you
figure it out yourself?

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:06.600
What?!

00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:11.700
There is no need for us to be together
now that Nene's gone.

00:20:13.666 --> 00:20:15.526
Which means...

00:20:15.933 --> 00:20:18.433
It's goodbye?

00:20:18.700 --> 00:20:21.500
Give me a break!
Nobody told me that!

00:20:22.000 --> 00:20:25.470
There are so many people
I still need to protect!

00:20:25.866 --> 00:20:30.626
And how are you going to
protect those people?

00:20:30.966 --> 00:20:35.166
I don't know how!
But if we stick together...

00:20:35.333 --> 00:20:37.233
Without Zola, what can we do?

00:20:37.766 --> 00:20:43.166
In the end, we can't do
anything without her.

00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:45.200
Shut up!

00:20:45.366 --> 00:20:49.366
Forget it. I don't want to get
involved in your "hero game."

00:20:49.666 --> 00:20:50.996
What?

00:20:51.700 --> 00:20:53.230
Stop it, you guys!

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:03.200
Jiro...

00:21:04.833 --> 00:21:06.833
I don't need to be here.

00:21:07.666 --> 00:21:10.826
Since I don't have a place to
go back to, I can go anywhere.

00:21:11.366 --> 00:21:14.466
That's too sudden!
Wait a minute...

00:21:20.733 --> 00:21:22.073
Where are you going?

00:21:29.600 --> 00:21:30.600
Zola...

00:21:31.633 --> 00:21:33.103
Don't rush by yourself.

00:21:34.266 --> 00:21:36.626
I hope all of you
are ready, too.

00:21:37.400 --> 00:21:38.400
Maro?

00:21:38.800 --> 00:21:42.270
I bet you rested well.
Let's get going.

00:21:42.500 --> 00:21:44.600
Huh? Isn't the journey over?

00:21:44.966 --> 00:21:46.696
Who ever said that?

00:21:47.066 --> 00:21:49.096
We still have some
loose ends to tie up.

00:21:49.333 --> 00:21:51.033
What do we need to do?

00:21:51.633 --> 00:21:52.673
You'll find out
when we get there.

00:21:52.900 --> 00:21:54.670
Where to, maro?

00:21:55.600 --> 00:21:56.930
To the Sealed Grounds.

00:22:34.000 --> 00:22:36.370
I see you have
increased your powers.

00:22:36.800 --> 00:22:37.470
Yes.

00:22:37.733 --> 00:22:40.303
So what is our next move?

00:22:41.000 --> 00:22:42.000
Ah, yes...

00:24:18.733 --> 00:24:20.533
Logi appears before
Shu and the others.

00:24:20.700 --> 00:24:22.770
His relationship to Zola
is finally revealed.

00:24:22.966 --> 00:24:26.626
They were not just lovers
but are blood-related siblings!

00:24:26.733 --> 00:24:30.573
Their real father is Nene?!
So that's why they tried to defeat him!

00:24:30.600 --> 00:24:32.030
Such a love-hate drama, maro.

00:24:32.066 --> 00:24:34.726
That's melodrama,
not Blue Drama.

00:24:34.833 --> 00:24:37.273
Next on Blue Dragon:
Rosekstan
